  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Hardened the adaptive integrator against principal-value false success, partial initial partitions, affine overflow and endpoint-coordinate collapse, callback-side budget overruns, and permissive independent validation. Whole-line halves now adapt separately; every nonconverged solver stop suppresses the primary value while preserving any complete-partition scalar only as an explicitly unvalidated solver estimate; validation preserves the solver termination record; exact elapsed-time status/diagnostics align with the shared contract. The manifest-discovered CPython/Sage.js laboratory and SciPy/mpmath oracle cover adversarial odd divergence, cancellation, budgets, callback failures, huge and adjacent finite intervals, reversed and oscillatory cases, and deterministic narrow-feature blind spots. Documentation and capability metadata state the qualified numerical and platform envelope without unearned release claims.",
    "risks": [
      "The exact maximum_elapsed_time result depends on central shared-contract commit 52d91d862 (status and diagnostic registry); this lane intentionally does not edit shared registries.",
      "Binary64 cannot resolve arbitrarily translated endpoint-singularity coordinates; the implementation now fails explicitly with interval_too_small instead of sampling an endpoint or claiming success.",
      "Deterministic embedded and independent quadrature rules can jointly miss an unbracketed feature narrower than their sampled nodes; this limitation is documented and regression-demonstrated."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Integrate the central package ownership, registry, pyright, and maximum_elapsed_time shared-contract changes, then rerun the manifest integration tier.",
      "Collect browser, SEA, Linux arm64, macOS arm64, and Windows x64 receipts before changing the development-only platform qualification."
    ]
  }
